  "question": {
    "text": "The angle of elevation of the top of a tower from a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> due north of it is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and from a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;units due west of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math>. If the distance of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> from the tower is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> units, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cot</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
